# 0001 · Pre-production: steps with nothing to act on are inactive

- Status: accepted
- Date: @@TODAY@@
- Guide version: @@GUIDE_VERSION@@
- Rules concerned: DEL-CI-001, DEL-REPO-002, FND-CONF-005, DEL-CD-003

## Context

The repository exists before any app conforms, before the signing key and the
servers exist. DEL-CI-001 makes every CI step mandatory and allows disabling one
only through an ADR.

## Decision

A step that has nothing to act on prints `inactive: <reason>` and passes:

| Step | Inactive while |
|---|---|
| `test-platform`, `test-backend`, `test-e2e` | no app is in `platform.lock` (or no core app with a Playwright configuration) |
| `sign` | the `COSIGN_PRIVATE_KEY` secret is not set |
| `renovate` | the `RENOVATE_TOKEN` secret is not set |

Every other step always runs. `just release` and `just deploy`, run on purpose,
fail with the missing precondition instead of passing.

## Consequences

- CI is green from the first commit while still running everything that can run.
- Each inactive step activates by itself when its precondition appears; nothing
  has to be switched on by hand.
- No release can be made while any of them is inactive for lack of an app or a
  key, so the shortcut never reaches production.

## Review

Remove this ADR, and the inactive branches, after the first platform release.
